From 32d485cb38c6bcac766d67297f5222fa78ca3d99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jurilw <washington.juri@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:35:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(composer): local dictation through the desktop app

A mic button in the composer records a prompt and inserts the transcript
at the caret. Transcription is done by a whisper.cpp whisper-server.

Why the desktop and not the T3 server: the server a patched desktop talks
to is often the official build (SSH environments on another host; the
iPhone app needs a current official server there). A server-side RPC would
mean patching and pinning that server. Instead the Electron main process
sends each clip itself, so dictation works against any server version:

- T3CODE_TRANSCRIBE_SSH_HOST=<ssh alias>: runs `ssh <host> curl ...` and
  pipes the clip to a whisper-server on that host's loopback
  (T3CODE_TRANSCRIBE_REMOTE_URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8178/inference).
  BatchMode, the user's own ssh config and keys; no tunnel or port to keep.
- otherwise HTTP to T3CODE_TRANSCRIBE_URL (default the same loopback URL
  on the desktop machine, e.g. a local server or a manual ssh -L).
- T3CODE_TRANSCRIBE_URL=off disables it.

The button is rendered only while the backend answers a probe (re-checked
every 30 s and on window focus, cached 15 s in the main process), and never
outside the desktop app, so web and mobile clients see nothing.

The recording lives in a module-level session store (one microphone, one
session) so layout changes cannot stop it: scrolling the timeline used to
rest the composer, unmount the button and drop the clip. An active session
also counts as expanded chrome, so the composer stays open while
dictating. Transcripts go to the composer that started the session; if it
is gone they are held, copied to the clipboard and inserted on return.

Tests: dictationSession.test.ts, dictationAvailability.test.ts (web),
whisperTranscription.test.ts (desktop).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
